                                                                    28 1451
  Temperatures = 293.6 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 1600 2000 K    28 1451
                                                                    28 1451
 HISTORY                                                            28 1451
 -------                                                            28 1451
 This evaluation was generated by Naval Nuclear Laboratory [1]      28 1451
 using FLASSH [2].  The physical model is based on a generalized    28 1451
 elastic scattering treatment and includes coherent elastic         28 1451
 scattering and inelastic scattering components at 10               28 1451
 temperatures.  The evaluation is intended to be used with the      28 1451
 companion C(Be2C) TSL evaluation when modeling beryllium           28 1451
 carbide.                                                           28 1451
                                                                    28 1451
 THEORY                                                             28 1451
 ------                                                             28 1451
 Beryllium carbide (Be2C) has a cubic anti-fluorite (CaF2)          28 1451
 crystallographic structure (Fm3m space group) with four            28 1451
 molecules per unit cell [3].  The coherent elastic scattering      28 1451
 cross sections were evaluated in the cubic approximation using     28 1451
 the FLASSH generalized elastic scattering treatment based on       28 1451
 the Be2C unit cell crystal structure [3], the measured room        28 1451
 temperate unit cell lattice parameter of 4.3420 Ang from [4]       28 1451
 and the Be and C free atom scattering cross sections from          28 1451
 ENDF/B-VIII.0.  The inelastic scattering cross sections were       28 1451
 evaluated in the incoherent approximation using the Be and C       28 1451
 phonon density of states from a first-principles VASP/PHONON       28 1451
 calculation [1] using a 3x3x3 supercell, a phonon order of 400,    28 1451
 and LO/TO splitting to better capture the higher energy            28 1451
 vibrational modes.                                                 28 1451
                                                                    28 1451
